Ok, good, glad you found something that worked. In general for a user-defined distribution in a package that depends on NIMBLE,
I think you want the distribution to be created such that it is an object in the namespace of your package.

The NIMBLE team is working currently on a couple packages that will depend on NIMBLE, so may one of the core developers might chime in here
with other thoughts on this topic in coming weeks.

Chris

